        "id": 120012,
        "name": "Comrade Bubbles",
        "username": "Comrade_Bubbles",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/comrade_bubbles/{size}/2007_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-03T11:30:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>That is an interesting distinction and is such an inherent part of the formula that I've also never really considered it.</p><p>On the other hand, by putting RPG elements like that in an adventure game, you're appealing to the demographic of gamers who like realism mixed with their escapism. If that makes sense. But it does mean that sometimes you might think you haven't solved the puzzle when the RNG doesn't go your way and give you a success.</p><p>That said, I wouldn't mind giving something like that a go. I think it might be an interesting take on the puzzle genre.</p>",
