        "raw": "<p>That is an interesting distinction and is such an inherent part of the formula that I&#39;ve also never really considered it.</p><p>On the other hand, by putting RPG elements like that in an adventure game, you&#39;re appealing to the demographic of gamers who like realism mixed with their escapism. If that makes sense. But it does mean that sometimes you might think you haven&#39;t solved the puzzle when the RNG doesn&#39;t go your way and give you a success.</p><p>That said, I wouldn&#39;t mind giving something like that a go. I think it might be an interesting take on the puzzle genre.</p>",
