        "id": 120013,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-03T13:47:57.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>That is one of the things I dislike about RPG video games. &nbsp;The world is never dynamic enough to feel real, and the closer they get with the newer games, the more and more the failure stand out. &nbsp;At least it does to me.</p><p>In that way I prefer adventure games because the solution to puzzles is to solve the puzzle, not to go level a skill for a month while the shop keper continues to search for a potion that for some reason I can't just tell her is in a tree so she can get a ladder and go on with her life.</p>",
